From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:26:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t7000-6: Add the D2186 PMIC ADC

The iPhone 6 and 6 Plus (N61, N56) have the iPod touch 6's Dialog D2186
PMIC at the same address (pmic@74, the D2186 GPIO block already
described). Describe its housekeeping ADC there too, so the battery and
bus voltages, the charge and bus currents and the battery thermistor read
through IIO on those phones as well.

The battery itself stays with the bq27540 gauge these phones have; an
apple,d2186-battery node would register the same battery a second time.

Untested on the N61 and N56.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-6.dtsi | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-6.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-6.dtsi
index 10b5f3e..6dba0fa 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-6.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t7000-6.dtsi
@@ -96,6 +96,18 @@
 			nvmem-cell-names = "rtc_offset";
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * The PMIC's housekeeping ADC, as on the iPod touch 6. The
+		 * iPhone 6 has a bq27540 gauge for the battery, so no
+		 * apple,d2186-battery node: it would report the same battery
+		 * a second time.
+		 */
+		pmu_adc: adc@500 {
+			compatible = "apple,d2186-adc";
+			reg = <0x500 0x24>;
+			#io-channel-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		nvmem@4000 {
 			compatible = "apple,pmic-nvmem";
 			reg = <0x4000 0x28>;
